! ==================================================
! General blocks
! ==================================================
||proxystream.st^
!
! ==================================================
! BBC iPlayer - force IPv4 (block AAAA records only)
! ==================================================
! Why: iPlayer traffic is policy-routed on pfSense via the
! site-to-site WireGuard tunnel to Pts (branch) and out their WAN.
! Pts has no IPv6, so the tunnel can only carry IPv4.
! Blocking AAAA makes devices use IPv4 for BBC, so they hit the
! pfSense rule matching alias urls_to_route_branch_vpn.
! A records are NOT blocked, so iPlayer still works normally.
! Related: pfSense IPv6 Reject rules on LAN and WG_ROADWARRIOR.
! Remove these lines if Pts gets IPv6 or the routing is removed.
!
! BBC domains (each rule covers all subdomains)
||bbc.co.uk^$dnstype=AAAA
||bbci.co.uk^$dnstype=AAAA
||bbc.com^$dnstype=AAAA
!
! iPlayer CDN hostnames (keep in sync with the pfSense alias list)
||vod-dash-uk-live.akamaized.net^$dnstype=AAAA
||vod-hls-uk-live.akamaized.net^$dnstype=AAAA
||vod-thumb-uk-live.akamaized.net^$dnstype=AAAA
